# Hand-decided substantive judgments. Input hashes merely bind these decisions.
rows=[
('ce19b80f','KEEP','KEEP','The proposed modelled structure/function relationship removes a second AP-generation competence from this atom. Reception, long-distance conduction and output transmission are linked to the supplied neuronal structures; the DE/EN statements agree.','The labelled-structure case requires connecting structures to function. The disconnected-terminal transfer separates successful conduction in the same neuron from transmission to another.','Structure/function is one assessable causal relationship; AP particle mechanisms remain on04d, resting mechanisms on e3fb and fibre comparison on080.','The structure legend supplies vocabulary; functional reasoning, rather than unsupported name recall, is assessed.','HE GK1 structure component and BY13 outline/structure-function support this candidate. BY8 entire sense→nervous→effector chain and lower investigations are larger clauses; preserving them on reviewed partners is required.'),
('ff1bf88f','KEEP','KEEP','Chemical versus electrical transmission and transmitter effects are scientifically sound and form a comparison at the same transmission level; neither mode is inferred from an electrical impulse alone.','Vesicle-release intervention distinguishes chemical from direct electrical transmission. The ACh-breakdown case predicts longer receptor exposure under the given excitatory model, without a universal excitatory-ACh rule.','A common transmission question can compare the two mechanisms; exact source coverage for both is a separate limitation.','Diagrams, molecule labels and intervention facts are supplied; explaining causal propagation needs no separate recall deck.','HE GK2 establishes an excitatory ACh chemical component, voltage-/ligand-dependent channels and NMJ, not electrical synapses. No audited lower relation supports the full two-mode goal. Preserve substance application, channel and motor-endplate clauses in suitable source-specific components.'),
('a46cafde','KEEP','REVISE','The proposed same-input/different-effective-connection explanation is a defensible model application. It is distinct from describing a cellular change347, integrating instantaneous potentials e111 and analysing convergence/divergence97. All three original levels need retained routes.','Both cases positively explain changed network output: strengthening A changes its effect, while a stronger inhibitory input can counter a local strengthening. The essential DE/EN text additionally contains internal review bookkeeping, which is not learner understanding and must be removed.','One causal model relation between changed effective connections and input processing is assessable. Its placement is a derived learning application, not a new literal HE GK bullet.','The supplied network rules remove any need to memorise unprovided circuitry or algorithms.','HE LK5 cellular learning is a contextual derivation, not an exact network bullet or GK requirement. TH lower strengthening/deactivation as a learning foundation must be retained at its elementary depth; no wholesale upper task transfer is approved.'),
('78748ef2','KEEP','KEEP','Graded receptor potentials and the functional difference between primary and secondary sensory cells can be described as one input-to-neural-signal organisation problem. Both languages have the same scope.','A cell with its own axon versus a cell signalling to a separate neuron identifies primary/secondary organisation. A supplied hyperpolarisation mechanism prevents the false rule that all receptor potentials depolarise.','Two sensory-cell organisations instantiate the same receptor-to-neural-signal competence.','Cell schemes and legends provide the names; structural/functional comparison is the assessed performance.','HE LK1/LK2 support these components. BY13 EA demands particle-level generation plus sensory-physiology applications, with rhodopsin/retinal, hyperpolarisation/regeneration and temporal resolution/afterimages in contents. These broader clauses are not fully covered by the current description/cases.'),
('19758e09','KEEP','KEEP','Joint neural/endocrine information control is a coherent systems explanation; receptor selectivity prevents a claim that one hormone necessarily affects every tissue.','A fast neural gland trigger followed by hormone targets explains coupled routes. Blocking one target receptor while upstream hormone remains separates target response from secretion.','Coupling two signalling modes addresses one shared regulatory process. The comparison operator and named stress axes require their own explicit coverage.','Pathway and receptor facts are supplied; explaining their relationship does not require separate memorisation of a hormone inventory.','HE LK3 supports coupling. BY8 hormone modelling and comparison, BY13 EA stress-axis comparison, and HH/NW comparisons must remain explicit. Puberty-only clauses do not justify full coupling. Full ff1 as a lower prerequisite needs a later actual source-view/frontier check.'),
('e1117126','KEEP','KEEP','The new DE/EN sentence explicitly links spatial/temporal excitatory and inhibitory integration to AP generation. This corrects the old title/description operator mismatch without claiming exact real-membrane linearity.','In the declared additive model −70+8+10−5=−57mV does not reach−55mV; removing−5 gives−52mV. The fresh timing/interference trace tests overlap and decay, not just memorised EPSP/IPSP definitions.','One threshold-integration relationship connects spatial and temporal cases; this is not a bundle of unrelated terms.','Trace labels, rest and threshold values are given; reasoning about combined inputs is decisive.','HE LK4 and BY13 EA integration support the core. The required inhibition/regulation meaning is visible in the before/without-inhibition contrast. Keep it in LK/EA and do not infer a lower or GK obligation from network vocabulary.'),
('347110a1','KEEP','KEEP','Functional and structural cellular plasticity are scientifically coherent examples of cellular learning mechanisms; the text does not require an individual memory diagnosis.','Persistent response change under the same weak test/control supports functional change without identifying molecules. New contacts with constant individual strength distinguish structural from functional plasticity.','One persistent cellular connection-change competence can compare these two forms.','Model observations and labels are supplied; distinguishing changes and their consequences needs no independent catalogue recall.','HE LK5 supports cellular learning. BY13 EA additionally requires explaining why plasticity is necessary for learning, not only classifying observations. Retain that reasoning through347 with a46 processing consequences. TH elementary strengthening/deactivation is a separate depth-preservation obligation.'),
('485ef1c3','REVISE','KEEP','The unchanged claim to explain neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer is broader than the HE principle/example requirement and the bounded models tested. Bind the text explicitly to principle-level supplied disorder models; disease-wide clinical explanation is not demonstrated.','Connection-loss/processing relation is explained in an expressly provided Alzheimer model. A structural degenerative change versus temporary transmitter change correctly prevents identical-function→identical-cause diagnosis.','A bounded neuronal disturbance→functional effect relationship is atomic. The current open-ended disease-wide wording must first be bounded.','Disease features are supplied in the case model; no unsupported diagnostic criteria or clinical recall deck is justified.','HE LK6 supports a neuronal-system disturbance principle using an example. BY Depression and MS/Parkinson exact relations are BLOCK: no substitution by Alzheimer. Preserve each named disorder and the depression multifactorial/therapy/social duties on actually suitable components.'),
('afde0001','KEEP','KEEP','Describing one brain-imaging principle is an appropriate bounded method competence; fMRI and structural MRI are not electrical recordings or direct thought measurements.','The supplied fMRI signal is indirect haemodynamic contrast. A fresh structural/functional-method selection explains what each can answer without automatic diagnosis. NIMH independently supports the stated signal/interpretation limits.','Method principle, output and inference limit form one assessable method relationship.','The imaging principle is provided as material; interpreting it does not require an independent modality-name deck.','HE LK7 supports one brain-imaging principle. BY13 EA electrical diagnostic methods, with ENG/EKG in contents, are not an exact imaging relation. Preserve those actual diagnostic obligations; no current matching complete ordinary atom was found.'),
('2381d2bb','KEEP','KEEP','Changing only the title to planning/evaluating potential measurements aligns it with the existing DE/EN description. A model plan cannot certify actual laboratory execution.','The model recording plan identifies reference, controlled stimulus, time course and conditions. The fresh reversed-polarity trace requires recognising a sign convention issue rather than inventing changed cell physiology.','Planning and evaluating the same potential measurement form one evidence-generation competence.','Instrumentation labels and traces are given; causal planning/evaluation is decisive, not device-name recall.','HE GK3 says potential measurements without the previous authored perform verb. The candidate is a reasonable model operationalisation, while practical source operators elsewhere remain unproved. Keep lower real investigations separately. BY ENG/EKG medical diagnosis is a larger different method requirement.'),
('c9a06264','KEEP','KEEP','LTP/LTD as sustained changes and their experimental classification are sound at the model level; a response increase is not proof of a particular person’s memory or all molecular mechanisms.','Same-test2→5 sustained versus control2 supports an LTP-consistent observation. Sustained4→2 versus recovery4 distinguishes LTD-consistent change from a transient effect.','Long-term direction of synaptic response change is one experimental comparison competence.','The traces supply baselines, time and controls; classifying persistence and inference does not need separate abbreviation recall.','HE LK5 permits this didactic cellular-learning specialization but does not name LTP/LTD as a separate compulsory bullet. Mark it as an authored specialization, preserving cellular learning rather than multiplying literal source duties.'),
('4f631f78','KEEP','KEEP','Applying a supplied artificial Hebbian rule and discussing its bounded implications is legitimate modelling; its weights are not asserted biological measured constants.','WithΔw=.1xy, .3 plus two coactive pairs gives .5. The fresh unlimited repetition case positively predicts growth and explains why a bounded rule is needed, rather than claiming all learning follows it.','Application and model-limit analysis concern the same given update rule.','Formula, activity values and starting weight are provided; no memorised formula/card prerequisite is implied.','HE LK5 is a contextual didactic link. Hebbian rules are not literally named on page43; retain this as a declared specialization whose curricular placement still needs author rationale, not a fictitious original bullet.'),
('97b24279','KEEP','KEEP','Convergence/divergence analysis is coherent network topology reasoning, distinct from e111 instantaneous integration and a46 altered effective connections.','The three-to-one/one-to-three contrast explains pooling/distribution and identifies missing threshold factors. The fresh mixed excitatory/inhibitory outputs explain why a common input does not force identical outputs.','One topology-to-information-routing competence covers both inverse patterns.','Legended graphs supply terms and connections; analysis does not require an independent wiring lexicon deck.','HE LK4 is related to integration, but named convergence/divergence is not a literal page43 list item. Keep a bounded topology application and the real synaptic integration duty; do not claim whole source identity.'),
('9b966664','KEEP','KEEP','Receptor/context-dependent modulatory effects can be explained without the unsupported rule that a transmitter universally activates or causes a psychiatric disease.','Given dopamine receptor variants explain opposite local effects. A fresh serotonin threshold modification supports model-level signalling while an uncontrolled behavioural association cannot establish a sole human cause.','The same context-dependent modulation relationship is assessed across two examples.','Receptor and effect information are provided; an exhaustive transmitter inventory is unnecessary.','HE LK3 names hormones and interplay, not a dopamine/serotonin-system bullet; its proposed contextual link is weak and must not substitute for hormone action. BY depression serotonin facts can contribute only a component; no multifactorial/clinical/social coverage follows.'),
('f6280154','KEEP','KEEP','Synapse-level effects of supplied substances are bounded mechanistic neuropharmacology; no dose, treatment or organism-wide prediction is demanded.','Receptor blockade with preserved release predicts absent postsynaptic response. Reuptake inhibition with receptors intact predicts prolonged availability under otherwise equal conditions.','Intervention at transmission steps forms one causal competence across differing sites of action.','The substance intervention facts are given; a drug-name memory inventory is not required.','HE GK2 requires one example of ACh substance action, including NMJ, whereas this old LK-targeted broader psychoactive goal is not whole-GK2 evidence. Preserve a suitable common-GK ACh/motor/channel component, rather than treating all psychoactive mechanisms as mandatory.'),
('8b23f8fb','KEEP','REVISE','The existing stimulus-to-signal-to-code competence can remain with its stable ID, provided generation and information representation are both visibly assessed. Coding terms alone do not demonstrate transduction.','The5/15 equal-height impulses correctly test frequency code and the fresh group patterns test place/population code. Neither case asks the learner to explain stimulus→channel/receptor-potential→neural-signal generation, despite its essential expectation and goal text.','An explicitly linked input-conversion/representation pipeline is coherent; retaining an unassessed conversion half is not acceptable P coverage.','Patterns, labels and provided transduction mechanics can support reasoning; no separate unprompted coding-term recall deck is necessary.','HE Q2.4 contains one sense-organ transduction context; three codes are not named and are not a literal Q2.3 LK16 bullet. BY13 EA receptor/eye particle and sensory-phenomena clauses must be retained on appropriate sensory partners.'),
('1b38144f','KEEP','KEEP','Fluid mosaic structure and selective transport are a coherent membrane structure/function relationship; active routes require energy and are not equated to passive diffusion.','The supplied A-channel/B-pump model distinguishes down-gradient and energy-coupled routes. Blocking A while B and neutral C remain explains route selectivity. For future rendered material, specify neutral A or negligible electrical gradient rather than generalising concentration direction to all ions.','One membrane architecture-to-transport competence can contrast different specified routes.','Models state substance/protein properties and gradients; mechanistic use of them does not require protein-name recall.','BY13 EA/GA explicitly support the fluid-mosaic/transport goal. HE GK1 provides prerequisite context rather than a separate full membrane bullet. Keep BY direct evidence and do not relabel the HE prerequisite as an original independent duty.'),
('e3fb5f1d','KEEP','KEEP','Ion distributions, small membrane charge separation and maintained energy-dependent gradients are scientifically separated from bulk compartments becoming charged.','The supplied K-permeable high-inside model explains diffusion opposed by the developing electrical force. Pump interruption with initially retained gradients distinguishes maintenance from an obligatory instantaneous collapse.','Charge-generation and maintained gradients are linked parts of one resting-potential causal explanation.','Ion data, directions and permeability are supplied; no concentration-number or pump-name deck is required.','HE GK1 resting component and BY13 EA/GA data-to-charge/energy operator support this core. No exact numerical membrane potential is derived from insufficient ion data.'),
('04d770b3','KEEP','KEEP','AP particle dynamics and impulse coding are a coherent membrane-event-to-information relationship; the sodium-potassium pump is not claimed as the immediate repolarisation mechanism.','The supplied channel/trace model explains Na inward, delayed K outward and threshold dependence. More equal-height spikes plus a no-refire interval test frequency encoding and refractory limitation.','Mechanism and the signal form produced by that mechanism are assessable together.','Channel timings and trace legend are supplied; reasoning does not depend on recalling a universal numerical threshold.','HE GK1 AP and BY13 EA/GA AP/coding support this text. BY contents additionally name absolute/relative refractory phases and stimulus intensity/duration; keep both distinctions in the actual taught/source component, without claiming these42 briefs already exhaust every clause.'),
('080b10c7','KEEP','KEEP','Controlled fibre comparison explains functional conduction consequences while avoiding the false claim that all invertebrates have one fibre type or all vertebrates another.','For1m at10/50m/s the synthetic times are .1/.02s. Myelin means faster passive internodal spread with AP regeneration at nodes, not particles jumping nodes. The fresh confounded animal comparison prevents assigning all speed differences to myelin alone.','One controlled mechanism-to-performance comparison includes its applicable animal inference limits.','Length/speeds and fibre properties are supplied; classification of all animal fibres is not a recall requirement.','HE GK1 conduction and BY13 EA/GA fibre-performance operator support this core. BY costs/benefits and actual invertebrate/vertebrate comparisons must remain visible where that source component is adopted; model timing alone is not a complete energetic-cost study.'),
('c05e217f','KEEP','REVISE','Hormonconcentration regulation and a specified effect on another hormonal loop form a coherent coupled-feedback question. The unchanged EN feedback-loop claim matches the DE regulatory-loop meaning.','Case1 correctly explains negative cortisol feedback without negative concentrations. Case2 supplies only cortisol→glucose availability; that one-way link does not specify the second hormonal feedback loop which task and expected answer claim to explain. Add its actual hormone/target/feedback model and ask for a bounded causal effect.','A source-specified perturbation of linked loops is assessable, but the second loop must exist in the material.','Curves and loop arrows are supplied; no endocrine catalogue or disease-diagnosis recall deck is justified.','BY13 EA directly supports cortisol regulation and intervention into glucose regulation; GA does not name this EA duty. HE LK3 is contextual hormone action, not an explicit chronic-stress bullet. Raw GK tags cannot establish GA/GK coverage.')]
